\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\sl-480\slmult0\tx720\tx4752{\f0\fs24 \cf1 {\v \u9484? The other issue I'm thinking about is abbreviations.  Today, the\line}{\v \u9474? Chicago Manual of Style recommends leaving periods out of USA,\line}{\v \u9474? US, UN, and degrees such as PhD; they also say you should no\line}{\v \u9474? longer treat abbreviated "Junior" or "Senior" as a parenthetical\line}{\v \u9474? (and so shouldn't surround it by commas):  Roy Wood Jr. -- not\line}{\v \u9474? Roy Wood, Jr., with commas -- would be the current CMS style.\line}{\v \u9474? But those LOOK modern, and I think in this novel, I'll use the\line}{\v \u9474? forms of abbreviation that were common in the 1940s and 1950s:\line}{\v \u9474? J. Robert Oppenheimer, Ph.D., born in the U.S.A., lived to see\line}{\v \u9492? the rise of the U.N.\line}}\par
